verl
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `verl/` directory is a vendored copy of verl (version 0.7.0.dev, see
`verl/verl/version/version`), from:

    https://github.com/volcengine/verl

Copyright 2023-2024 Bytedance Ltd. and/or its affiliates
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

It is shipped in full rather than as a patch so that `pip install -e ./verl`
works against the cloned tree. Modifications made for this work are listed in
`docs/verl_changes.md`; the upstream license and notice are retained at
`verl/LICENSE` and `verl/Notice.txt`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prune-OPD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is built on the Prune-OPD release, from:

    https://github.com/yangzhch6/Prune-OPD

Prune-OPD: Efficient and Reliable On-Policy Distillation for Long-Horizon
Reasoning, Yang et al., 2026 (arXiv:2605.07804). The token-level top-k overlap
compatibility criterion and the surrounding `prune_opd` module originate there;
Flash-OPD reuses the criterion and compares against Prune-OPD as a baseline.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPD (THUNLP)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The on-policy distillation objective in this repository -- the
`token_reward_direct` advantage estimator, the student top-k candidate set, and
the use of the teacher as a scoring model -- derives from:

    https://github.com/thunlp/OPD

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Datasets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`datasets/` redistributes third-party evaluation and training data for
reproducibility. Each remains under the license of its original release:

    dapo-math-17k                 DAPO (BytedTsinghua-SIA)
    AMC23, AIME24, AIME25         competition problem sets
    HMMT24, HMMT25                competition problem sets
    MATH-500                      MATH (Hendrycks et al.) test subset
    Minerva                       Minerva Math (Lewkowycz et al.)
    Olympiad-Bench                OlympiadBench (He et al.)
    GPQA                          GPQA (Rein et al.)

The `ood250/` subdirectories are fixed 250-prompt subsets of the corresponding
test sets, shipped so the transfer evaluation uses the same prompts the paper
reports.
